This product is an independent, clean-room implementation of public protocols.
It contains no code, resources or assets from any commercial download manager.

Protocols implemented from their public specifications:
  · HTTP Range requests / resumption — RFC 9110, RFC 9111
  · Content-Disposition filenames — RFC 6266, RFC 5987
  · HTTP Live Streaming — RFC 8216
  · MPEG-DASH — ISO/IEC 23009-1
  · Model Context Protocol — public MCP spec (JSON-RPC 2.0)

Runtime: Node.js built-ins only (>= 20.11). No third-party packages are
required at runtime; the test-suite uses node:test (stdlib).

Trademarks: "Internet Download Manager", "IDM", "1DM+" and all other product
names belong to their owners and are used descriptively only. This project is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of them.

Reference analysis: the feature checklist in docs/PARITY.md was derived from
static inspection of an APK's public AndroidManifest.xml (package, version,
permissions, components, intent filters). No decompilation, resource extraction
or traffic capture was performed.
